  "scope_id": "CORRECTIONS-20261026-001",
  "title": "SL(2,3) is polynomial with bounded homology; the line is the twisting, not the Fitting height",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups with bounded first homology into finite solvable groups",
  "conclusion": "SL(2,3) is polynomial on closed 3-manifolds with bounded first homology: its maps are A4 maps forming affine twisted-cocycle spaces, and the central lift is obstructed by a quadratic function into the bounded group H^2(M; F2), counted by Gauss sums. The bounded-homology line is not the Fitting height: UT3(F4) x| C3, also of Fitting height 2, is #P-hard because its twisted obstruction is a free three-way form.",
